# XForms (Forms Library) — Athena-style import for motif-on-qt

This directory holds (or will hold) the genuine XForms 1.2.4 library sources,
imported the same way libXaw lives under `src/xaw/`.

## Status (transition)

- **Goal**: compile the original XForms sources against motif-on-qt’s Xlib-on-Qt
  (and eventually thin-shim the public API over Qt widgets, see
  `docs/xview-xforms-shims.md`).
- **Current**: scaffolding + minimal `config.h`. Drop the official sources here
  and wire them into the top-level CMakeLists when ready.

## How to import the sources

Official release (LGPL 2.1):

  https://download-mirror.savannah.gnu.org/releases/xforms/xforms-1.2.4.tar.gz

```bash
# from the motif-on-qt top level
curl -L -o /tmp/xforms-1.2.4.tar.gz \
  https://download-mirror.savannah.gnu.org/releases/xforms/xforms-1.2.4.tar.gz
tar xzf /tmp/xforms-1.2.4.tar.gz -C /tmp
# copy library sources (keep our config.h and this README)
cp -a /tmp/xforms-1.2.4/lib/* src/xforms/
# restore our minimal config (or merge)
# cp path/to/our/config.h src/xforms/config.h
cp /tmp/xforms-1.2.4/COPYING.LIB /tmp/xforms-1.2.4/Copyright src/xforms/
```

Public headers live under `src/xforms/include/` (they become the installed
`<forms.h>` / individual class headers once packaging is added).

## Build notes (future CMake)

- Compile the `.c` files in this directory (and `private/` is private headers only).
- Include path: `src/xforms` and `src/xforms/include` plus the project’s
  `include/` (our X11 headers).
- Link against the motif-on-qt static archive (which supplies Xlib, Xpm, etc.).
- Optional: also pull in `image/` from the tarball if flimage support is wanted.
- Do **not** patch the XForms sources for missing Xlib; fix gaps in
  `src/xlib.cpp` (same rule as Athena).

## Minimal config.h

The supplied `config.h` is a hand-written stub sufficient for an initial
compile against a modern Unix + our Xlib. Expand `#define`s as the linker
or compiler report missing features.

## License

XForms is LGPL 2.1 (see COPYING.LIB once imported). Compatible with the
project’s own LGPL 2.1+.

## Next steps after sources are present

1. Add a CMake option (e.g. `MQ_BUILD_XFORMS`) and a static library target.
2. Resolve any missing Xlib symbols that the real sources call.
3. Bridge `fl_do_forms` / the XForms event model to the Qt event loop
   (or run it on top of our XEvent delivery).
4. Smoke-test with the demos from the tarball under
   `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen MOTIFQT_AUTOQUIT=…`.
